        {
          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/python-3.12@3.12.13-r3?distro=dhi-3.23"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update python-3.12 to 3.12.13-r4 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6100: lzma.LZMADecompressor, bz2.BZ2Decompressor and zlib decompression objects (used by gzip.GzipFile) could use freed memory when a decompression call failed with MemoryError and the object was reused. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/148395 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/ea8d735eb084cf8cc021df1a30e90d10a8f052e3), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6100. Checked the machine code of the _lzma, zlib and _bz2 extension modules in the python-3.12 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.16-r4, x86_64 and aarch64, comparing each architecture's disassembly; both architectures agree. The fix is a one-line change to each module. The _lzma and zlib code in 3.12.13-r4 and every later build is identical to that in the 3.12.14 builds, which contain the upstream fix, and differs from 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.13-r3. _bz2 changes in the same build, and again at 3.12.13-r10 for a separate bz2 fix (https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/150599), after which it matches the 3.12.14 builds. The range ends at 3.12.13-r4."
    },
