      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6100: lzma.LZMADecompressor, bz2.BZ2Decompressor and the internal zlib decompressor kept a dangling input pointer after a MemoryError, so a later decompress() call could read or write through a pointer to the already-released caller buffer. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/148395 (3.14 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/6a5f79c8d7bbf22b083b240910c7a8781a59437d), first released in CPython 3.14.5; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/HTWB2Z6KT5QQX4RYEZAFININDHNOSIF3/; https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6100. The fix is a one-line change to the error path of each decompressor and leaves nothing to detect in the _bz2, _lzma and zlib extension modules, so the boundary rests on the build history: among the published builds of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, 3.14.4-r4 is the build that added a DHI backport of the upstream fix, the same build that first carries the DHI backports of the CVE-2026-4786 and CVE-2026-5713 fixes, which are visible in its Lib/webbrowser.py and _remote_debugging module; builds from CPython 3.14.5 on contain the upstream fix. Checked both on x86_64 and aarch64."
