      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-6100: lzma.LZMADecompressor, bz2.BZ2Decompressor and zlib decompression objects (used by gzip.GzipFile) could use freed memory when a decompression call failed with MemoryError and the object was reused. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/148395 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/ea8d735eb084cf8cc021df1a30e90d10a8f052e3), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-6100. Checked the machine code of the _lzma, zlib and _bz2 extension modules in the standard library shipped by these packages (libpython-3.12-stdlib and libpython-3.12-minimal) in every build published in the DHI Debian repository, 3.12.13-0 to 3.12.16-7, amd64 and arm64, comparing disassembly per architecture. The fix is a one-line change to each module. The _lzma and zlib code in every published build is identical to that in 3.12.14-0, which is built from CPython 3.12.14 and contains the upstream fix. The _bz2 code is the same from 3.12.13-0 to 3.12.13-6 and changes at 3.12.13-7 for a separate bz2 fix (https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/150599), after which it matches 3.12.14-0. Every published build has the fix, so the range ends at 3.12.13-0, the lowest published build."
